cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "InSites: AI-assisted heritage significance assessment under epistemic notation and expert governance"
abstract: >-
  InSites is an experimental assistant that carries out context-based
  significance assessment of heritage places. It runs as a prose
  specification executed by a language model stage by stage, with expert
  review between stages. Every claim carries a mark reporting its distance
  from the source evidence. This repository holds the current
  specification, the architecture documentation, and the research record
  behind the Heritage 4.0 paper.
type: software
message: >-
  If you use this system or the research record, please cite it. For the
  findings reported in the Heritage 4.0 paper, cite the tagged release
  tuba-study rather than a branch.
